[sighs]

7
00:01:25.795 --> 00:01:26.712
[gargles]

8
00:01:36.222 --> 00:01:37.264
[sighs]

9
00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:07.127
-You good. dog?
-Yeah. Waiting to hear from Wharton.

10
00:02:07.211 --> 00:02:08.212
Who's Wharton?

11
00:02:08.879 --> 00:02:10.339
Wanna hear something really cute?

12
00:02:11.715 --> 00:02:14.677
-I think I'm in love again.
-Aw. Is that who I heard over last night?

13
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.011
Oh. my God. You heard that?

14
00:02:16.095 --> 00:02:17.596
-Yeah.
-Yeah. you know

15
00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.015
the hot French foreign exchange student?
Her name...

16
00:02:20.099 --> 00:02:21.976
-No.
-...kinda rhymes with "cappuccino."

17
00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.980
Dude. relax. Why are you tweaking
over a summer camp?

18
00:02:27.648 --> 00:02:29.817
It is. uh... It's not a summer camp.

19
00:02:30.651 --> 00:02:32.862
It's the most elite program
of any business school.

20
00:02:32.945 --> 00:02:35.698
AKA my dream school. AKA fast track
to getting into that school.

21
00:02:35.781 --> 00:02:38.117
AKA the most important moment of my life.

22
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.203
-It's literally summer.
-Yeah. the summer before senior year.

23
00:02:41.287 --> 00:02:43.455
-Exactly. Who cares?
-College admissions officers.

24
00:02:43.539 --> 00:02:45.291
You're 17. You act like you're 30.

25
00:02:45.374 --> 00:02:49.211
Don't you think you're gonna regret
not spending your summer going buck wild?

26
00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:51.088
Not really. No.

27
00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.298
-Morning.
-Hi. Morning.

28
00:02:52.381 --> 00:02:54.133
-I got bagels.
-Thanks.

29
00:02:54.216 --> 00:02:55.718
Ooh. Hero.

30
00:02:56.302 --> 00:02:59.263
Okay. How we doing?
Have we heard from Wharton?

31
00:02:59.346 --> 00:03:01.140
Not yet.

32
00:03:01.223 --> 00:03:03.559
-And she's being really chill about it.
-Great.

33
00:03:03.642 --> 00:03:05.686
-[gasps]
-[Steven] What? Is that it?

34
00:03:07.897 --> 00:03:08.898
Yes? No?

35
00:03:09.481 --> 00:03:10.691
Hmm? Huh?

36
00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.152
[Connor] Did you get in?

37
00:03:13.235 --> 00:03:15.029
[Steven] Connor? She's crying.

38
00:03:15.112 --> 00:03:17.323
[Connor] I can't tell
if she's happy or devastated.

39
00:03:17.406 --> 00:03:18.490
How are you twins?

40
00:03:18.574 --> 00:03:20.910
-You guys--
-[Steven] Annie. are you okay?

41
00:03:20.993 --> 00:03:22.995
-Mmm-hmm. I'm just processing.
-[Steven] Okay.

42
00:03:25.039 --> 00:03:26.040
[Steven] Yeah?

43
00:03:26.916 --> 00:03:28.918
The end of the life
I once imagined for myself.

44
00:03:29.001 --> 00:03:32.004
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry. Hey. can I hug?

45
00:03:32.087 --> 00:03:32.922
-Please?
-Hmm. yeah.

46
00:03:33.005 --> 00:03:34.798
-Everything's over. It's okay.
-Okay.

47
00:03:35.382 --> 00:03:37.301
-Thank you. Um...
-I love you.

48
00:03:37.384 --> 00:03:39.803
-I think good on hug now.
-Okay. I'm out.

49
00:03:40.387 --> 00:03:42.389
Look. if they don't want you.
it's their loss.

50
00:03:42.473 --> 00:03:43.307
[Annie] It's literally...

51
00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:46.435
I love you so much for saying that.
thanks. But it's literally my loss.

52
00:03:46.518 --> 00:03:49.730
-Legitimately. in a literal sense.
-What if we look at it as a good thing?

53
00:03:49.813 --> 00:03:53.859
You know? You're 17. You deserve
to have some fun. You could travel.

54
00:03:53.943 --> 00:03:56.654
-You could go to Greece with Connor.
-Hey. whoa! No. no. no.

55
00:03:56.737 --> 00:03:58.948
-That's a trip for me and Capoochie.
-[Steven] Who?

56
00:03:59.031 --> 00:04:00.699
[Connor] Why don't you go to Thailand

57
00:04:00.783 --> 00:04:04.286
with your 100% heterosexual
straight boyfriend?

58
00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.914
I cannot break up with him
till he's ready to come out.

59
00:04:06.997 --> 00:04:09.208
We've been together since sixth grade.
Could be bi.

60
00:04:09.291 --> 00:04:12.378
-Fair.
-And her name is Capucine.

61
00:04:12.461 --> 00:04:14.421
If you'll give her HPV.
at least say it right.

62
00:04:14.505 --> 00:04:17.591
-I don't have HVP.
-I know you don't. You have HPV.

63
00:04:17.675 --> 00:04:20.344
Annie. I promise it'll be okay.
Try not to get too worked up.

64
00:04:20.427 --> 00:04:22.012
Especially over a summer camp.

65
00:04:23.639 --> 00:04:24.765
It's a summer program.

66
00:04:24.848 --> 00:04:26.517
-[coughs] Camp.
-Dude.

67
00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.311
[hesitates] Can we all...

68
00:04:29.395 --> 00:04:30.813
-Summer program.
-[Steven] Yeah.

69
00:04:30.896 --> 00:04:34.358
-Annie didn't get into the summer program.
-Camp.

70
00:04:34.441 --> 00:04:36.902
I messed it up again.
I'm so sorry. Uh-uh.

71
00:04:36.986 --> 00:04:38.112
It's a summer program.

72
00:04:39.446 --> 00:04:40.698
[Connor] Damn. you're right.

73
00:04:40.781 --> 00:04:42.074
-It's a summer camp.
-I agree.

74
00:04:42.157 --> 00:04:44.451
-[Connor] Did it again. Sorry.
-Summer program.

75
00:04:47.997 --> 00:04:51.000
Wait. Did I get my HPV vaccine?

76
00:04:51.083 --> 00:04:53.002
'Cause she's right.
This shit is everywhere.

77
00:04:53.085 --> 00:04:55.170
-You're good.
-Wait. No. Dad. for real.

78
00:04:55.254 --> 00:04:57.089
This shit gives you butthole cancer.

79
00:04:57.715 --> 00:04:58.549
Yeah. it does.

80
00:05:01.427 --> 00:05:03.345
Uh. symptoms for HPV.

81
00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:09.810
Let's watch Cynthia Erivo sing "Edelweiss"
at the Kennedy Center over and over.

82
00:05:09.893 --> 00:05:11.395
It is incredibly healing.

83
00:05:11.478 --> 00:05:12.604
I already did that.

84
00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:15.024
-What?
-Yeah. It didn't even help.

85
00:05:15.899 --> 00:05:18.986
-What am I gonna do this summer now?
-I don't know. You could...

86
00:05:20.112 --> 00:05:22.072
-start SSRIs?
-Yeah.

87
00:05:22.156 --> 00:05:24.241
But I feel I have
an addictive personality. so...

88
00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:29.329
You know what I could do?
I could come to Thailand with you now.

89
00:05:30.914 --> 00:05:32.416
[chuckles awkwardly]

90
00:05:35.169 --> 00:05:36.086
Oh.

91
00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:37.463
That could be cool.

92
00:05:37.546 --> 00:05:39.590
Is there a reason you wouldn't want me
to come?

93
00:05:39.673 --> 00:05:42.843
No. No. Not at all. I would love that.

94
00:05:43.969 --> 00:05:44.845
I guess I just...

95
00:05:45.596 --> 00:05:46.430
[clears throat]

96
00:05:47.014 --> 00:05:49.683
I guess I was kind of expecting
this summer to be like

97
00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.394
a "do our own thing" kinda vibe.

98
00:05:52.478 --> 00:05:54.480
I'm sorry. Are you. like...

99
00:05:56.315 --> 00:05:59.109
-saying we should break up for the summer?
-No.

100
00:05:59.443 --> 00:06:02.821
-[chuckling] Annie. no.
-Okay.

101
00:06:02.905 --> 00:06:06.200
What? No. I just...

102
00:06:07.826 --> 00:06:11.371
-Unless you wanna break up for the summer.
-Okay. Oliver. let's just...

103
00:06:11.455 --> 00:06:13.874
-Sure.
-It's all good. Are... What's happening?

104
00:06:13.957 --> 00:06:20.130
I would say you... uh...

105
00:06:20.756 --> 00:06:22.091
-'Sup. pimps?
-Connor!

106
00:06:22.716 --> 00:06:24.468
-Grandpa died.
-What?

107
00:06:24.551 --> 00:06:27.805
But not "grandpa" grandpa. Mom's dad.
The one who apparently sucks.

108
00:06:27.888 --> 00:06:29.223
I'm sorry. Sucked.

109
00:06:29.306 --> 00:06:32.101
What's up. Oliver? I love the haircut.

110
00:06:32.184 --> 00:06:34.228
Thanks. You guys have a second grandpa?

111
00:06:34.311 --> 00:06:36.688
Our mom's dad. But you know
how we can't talk about her

112
00:06:36.772 --> 00:06:38.899
because our dad gets dark and sad?

113
00:06:38.982 --> 00:06:42.194
The same thing goes with this grandpa.
We haven't seen him since Mom died.

114
00:06:42.277 --> 00:06:44.947
-So your entire lives?
-Yeah. Apparently. he was shady as fuck

115
00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.157
-and everyone hated him.
-How'd you know he died?

116
00:06:47.241 --> 00:06:49.993
Someone from a lawyer's office called
and started talking legal.

117
00:06:50.077 --> 00:06:52.621
And I was like. "Shit. Help.
I need a grown-up.

118
00:06:52.704 --> 00:06:54.289
-My sister will call you--"
-I will.

119
00:06:54.373 --> 00:06:57.126
You just need to leave 'cause we were
having a conversation.

120
00:06:57.209 --> 00:06:58.418
-You and me? No.
-Yeah.

121
00:06:58.502 --> 00:06:59.920
-Okay.
-No. we weren't.

122
00:07:00.003 --> 00:07:02.089
-No. we were. This is rude.
-And it's not...

123
00:07:03.048 --> 00:07:05.968
It's not as important
as the death of an estranged grandpa.

124
00:07:06.677 --> 00:07:07.886
Almost nothing is.

125
00:07:10.556 --> 00:07:12.432
-You guys should talk.
-Thank you.

126
00:07:12.933 --> 00:07:15.394
-I'm so sorry for your loss.
-Thanks.

127
00:07:18.147 --> 00:07:19.189
Okay. [grunts]

128
00:07:19.273 --> 00:07:20.149
[chuckles]

129
00:07:20.649 --> 00:07:21.900
-Love you. babe.
-Bye.

130
00:07:28.157 --> 00:07:29.366
[door opens]

131
00:07:30.492 --> 00:07:31.827
[door closes]

132
00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:34.288
-Was he finally about to come out?
-I'm gonna kill you.

133
00:07:34.371 --> 00:07:37.416
-No! [screams]
-I'm gonna end your fucking life!

134
00:07:41.753 --> 00:07:44.214
[Marjorie] Well.
thank you for meeting me.

135
00:07:44.798 --> 00:07:46.967
No personal notes
beyond these instructions.

136
00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.927
so I'll just get straight to it.

137
00:07:49.011 --> 00:07:52.097
All right. Gordon has left you. Steven.

138
00:07:53.223 --> 00:07:54.224
nothing.

139
00:07:54.933 --> 00:07:57.477
And to Connor and Annie Jacobson.

140
00:07:57.561 --> 00:08:00.063
Gordon has made you the beneficiaries
of his trust.

141
00:08:00.147 --> 00:08:02.566
which you'll gain control over
when you turn 18.

142
00:08:03.233 --> 00:08:04.526
Uh. it includes...

143
00:08:05.652 --> 00:08:07.988
property on a parcel of land in Canada.

144
00:08:08.071 --> 00:08:09.740
-He's Canadian?
-[Connor] Don't fuck with Canada.

145
00:08:09.823 --> 00:08:11.116
[Marjorie] Yes. In Muskoka.

146
00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:14.369
-I have for-real. like. wolf phobia.
-[Annie] Does that mean Mom was Canadian?

147
00:08:14.453 --> 00:08:18.207
-Accent's too thick. Don't understand it.
-Nobody here is Canadian. [clears throat]

148
00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:19.416
-Can we please...
-Yeah. Uh...

149
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.461
-Sorry.
-Gordon also left

150
00:08:23.253 --> 00:08:26.465
these letters for Annie and Connor.

151
00:08:26.548 --> 00:08:27.799
-Thank you very much.
-Sorry.

152
00:08:27.883 --> 00:08:28.967
Can we read the letters?

153
00:08:29.051 --> 00:08:31.053
We'll discuss this later.
I gotta get to work.

154
00:08:31.136 --> 00:08:34.139
-[Annie] Dad. those are for us.
-[Steven] Yeah. [clears throat]

155
00:08:34.223 --> 00:08:35.057
-Hey.
-Yes?

156
00:08:35.182 --> 00:08:37.351
Anything else about this matter
comes directly to me.

157
00:08:37.434 --> 00:08:38.727
You understand?

158
00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:39.645
Okay.

159
00:08:42.606 --> 00:08:46.693
And. again. I am so sorry
about your grandfather's passing.

160
00:08:46.944 --> 00:08:49.029
-It's fine. We didn't know him.
-[Annie] Connor.

161
00:08:50.364 --> 00:08:53.450
[slow piano music playing]

162
00:09:50.215 --> 00:09:51.633
Really? Your birthday?

163
00:09:53.677 --> 00:09:55.679
[suspenseful music playing]

164
00:10:13.822 --> 00:10:15.824
[slow music playing]

165
00:10:48.398 --> 00:10:49.441
[sputters]

166
00:10:49.524 --> 00:10:50.817
Okay. [clears throat]

167
00:10:53.695 --> 00:10:57.866
"Annie. My biggest regret
is not fighting harder to see you."

168
00:10:58.367 --> 00:11:00.035
"It wasn't because I didn't love you."

169
00:11:00.911 --> 00:11:04.414
"I shouldn't have agreed to the plan.
I'm sorry."

170
00:11:05.791 --> 00:11:08.377
"I hope Sterling Point
will reveal the truth."

171
00:11:14.508 --> 00:11:17.302
"It was your mother's favorite place
on earth." [inhales sharply]

172
00:11:17.386 --> 00:11:21.223
"But most importantly. Annie. find her."

173
00:11:22.391 --> 00:11:25.936
"She will need you after I'm gone.
Love. Gordon."

174
00:11:27.312 --> 00:11:30.023
[breathing heavily]

175
00:11:31.566 --> 00:11:33.110
[whispering] Fuck.

176
00:11:34.903 --> 00:11:35.737
[sighs]

177
00:11:38.407 --> 00:11:40.158
Thank you. baby. Should I say <i>"bonjour"?</i>

178
00:11:40.242 --> 00:11:41.410
It's <i>"merci."</i>

179
00:11:42.202 --> 00:11:43.495
[Annie] Hey. Connor.

180
00:11:43.578 --> 00:11:45.414
I really need to talk to you for a second.

181
00:11:46.164 --> 00:11:48.458
Oh. hi. Are you Capucine? Hi.

182
00:11:48.542 --> 00:11:50.460
I'm Annie. So nice to meet you.

183
00:11:50.544 --> 00:11:52.003
Her English isn't very good.

184
00:11:53.046 --> 00:11:54.881
-I'm fluent in English.
-What? No.

185
00:11:54.965 --> 00:11:56.800
-Yeah. God.
-Connor. I need you to focus

186
00:11:56.883 --> 00:11:58.885
'cause this is sort of a pressing issue.

187
00:11:59.469 --> 00:12:02.722
Gordon has been writing us letters
our entire lives. Dad hid 'em in a safe.

188
00:12:03.807 --> 00:12:04.724
Wait. We have a safe?

189
00:12:05.308 --> 00:12:07.561
Did you find diamonds in there?
Beautiful gems?

190
00:12:07.644 --> 00:12:10.814
Connor! The last letter that Gordon wrote.
he said. "Find her."

191
00:12:10.897 --> 00:12:13.358
-Find who?
-Exactly! Something's going on.

192
00:12:13.442 --> 00:12:15.735
We have to figure out
what's happening right now.

193
00:12:15.819 --> 00:12:19.197
He's not even biologically related to us.
Now he's dead. What does it matter?

194
00:12:19.281 --> 00:12:22.284
It doesn't matter to you that
Dad's been lying to us our entire lives?

195
00:12:22.367 --> 00:12:24.369
Oh. you guys are adopted.

196
00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:28.123
Yeah. Our parents tried to have kids.
but our dad shoots blanks. so...

197
00:12:28.206 --> 00:12:30.125
[Annie] He is my only biological relative.

198
00:12:32.586 --> 00:12:35.422
-I need to go to Canada.
-[Connor] If you're gonna dig into shit.

199
00:12:35.505 --> 00:12:36.715
go for it.

200
00:12:37.257 --> 00:12:39.050
but please don't ruin this for me.

201
00:12:39.134 --> 00:12:40.886
I'm not trying to ruin anything for you.

202
00:12:40.969 --> 00:12:43.513
But can you. like. cover for me

203
00:12:43.597 --> 00:12:44.806
if I were to go?

204
00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:48.101
-Say I'm in Thailand with Oliver.
-Yeah. sure. Whatever.

205
00:12:48.185 --> 00:12:50.896
We have to go pack
for our flight to Ibiza.

206
00:12:50.979 --> 00:12:53.815
-I thought you were going to Greece.
-Yes. Ibiza. Greece. Dumbass.

207
00:12:53.899 --> 00:12:54.733
Right.

208
00:12:54.816 --> 00:12:57.736
[slow piano music playing]

209
00:13:04.701 --> 00:13:06.161
[sighs]

210
00:13:07.078 --> 00:13:08.413
[whispering] Sorry. Dad.

211
00:13:09.873 --> 00:13:10.999
Sorry.

212
00:13:20.717 --> 00:13:22.886
["Lover Girl" by Laufey playing]

213
00:13:31.811 --> 00:13:34.439
Excuse me. Could I have a pillow
and a blanket. please?

214
00:13:34.523 --> 00:13:36.900
We only provide those on flights
longer than two hours.

215
00:13:36.983 --> 00:13:40.195
-but lemme see what I can find--
-The flight isn't longer than two hours?

216
00:13:40.278 --> 00:13:43.156
We're in New York City. ma'am.
Headed to Toronto.

217
00:13:44.991 --> 00:13:46.493
It's a 45-minute flight.

218
00:13:47.619 --> 00:13:49.788
-Forty-five minutes?
-[Avery] Uh-huh.

219
00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:51.831
To Canada?

220
00:13:52.332 --> 00:13:53.333
[Avery] Mmm-hmm.

221
00:13:54.376 --> 00:13:55.544
But I just took an Ambien.

222
00:14:02.634 --> 00:14:03.927
[seatbelt light beeps]

223
00:14:05.428 --> 00:14:06.721
[mouthing]

224
00:14:09.266 --> 00:14:12.227
[male pilot] <i>Flight attendants.</i>
<i>please prepare the cabin for landing.</i>

225
00:14:17.941 --> 00:14:19.776
[yawns]

226
00:14:21.695 --> 00:14:23.863
[propeller droning]

227
00:14:25.991 --> 00:14:27.742
[softly] Where the fuck am I?

228
00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:30.036
[male voice] Annie?

229
00:14:30.662 --> 00:14:32.872
-Yeah. Hi.
-Hi. yeah. Ellis. your pilot.

230
00:14:32.956 --> 00:14:34.833
-Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you too.

231
00:14:34.916 --> 00:14:37.127
I'll be flying you to Muskoka.
[chuckles]

232
00:14:38.837 --> 00:14:40.547
Um. can I take your stuff?

233
00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:43.174
-Thank you so much.
-Yeah. no worries. [grunts]

234
00:14:46.928 --> 00:14:48.054
Sorry. Hey.

235
00:14:49.598 --> 00:14:50.515
Oh. sorry.

236
00:14:51.391 --> 00:14:52.892
-We're goin' this way.
-Yeah.

237
00:14:52.976 --> 00:14:55.103
No. [chuckles] You're good.

238
00:14:56.438 --> 00:14:58.315
Please tell me
this isn't how we're getting there.

239
00:14:59.441 --> 00:15:01.901
[Ellis] No. No. hell no.
That's how we're getting there.

240
00:15:02.444 --> 00:15:03.612
The plane in the water?

241
00:15:03.695 --> 00:15:06.781
