716
00:40:57.539 --> 00:40:58.623
Yeah. Did they?

717
00:40:59.291 --> 00:41:02.169
-Oh. I thought so.
-Yeah. I guess they did. You know what? I...

718
00:41:02.961 --> 00:41:06.506
Actually. is your mom here?
I haven't seen Denise in so long.

719
00:41:06.590 --> 00:41:08.508
I would love to say hey to her.

720
00:41:08.592 --> 00:41:10.927
-Yeah. she's downstairs. God. let's go.
-Cool.

721
00:41:11.011 --> 00:41:12.012
She'd love to see you.

722
00:41:12.095 --> 00:41:13.513
[line ringing]

723
00:41:13.597 --> 00:41:14.681
Pick up.

724
00:41:14.764 --> 00:41:17.142
<i>Hey. this is Annie Jacobson.</i>
<i>leave a message.</i>

725
00:41:17.225 --> 00:41:18.059
Come on.

726
00:41:20.395 --> 00:41:23.857
Why have your fuckin' phones in your hands
all day if you don't even answer 'em?

727
00:41:25.775 --> 00:41:27.569
[line ringing]

728
00:41:30.071 --> 00:41:37.078
[dance music playing]

729
00:41:37.245 --> 00:41:40.165
<i>-Hey. it's Oliver. Leave a message.</i>
-Great. Great.

730
00:41:43.835 --> 00:41:45.212
Mother!

731
00:41:45.295 --> 00:41:46.588
There she is. Mom!

732
00:41:47.297 --> 00:41:48.673
-What?
-Look.

733
00:41:49.633 --> 00:41:51.760
-Hi.
-Oh. my. Annie Jacobson!

734
00:41:52.510 --> 00:41:53.887
Hi. Denise.

735
00:41:53.970 --> 00:41:58.225
The last time I saw you.
you hadn't even started your period yet.

736
00:41:58.308 --> 00:42:00.227
-[chuckles awkwardly]
-And I only know that

737
00:42:00.310 --> 00:42:01.937
because I asked your housekeeper.

738
00:42:02.020 --> 00:42:06.024
I was worried about you at that age.
You know. without a mom.

739
00:42:06.107 --> 00:42:06.942
[Rory] Mom...

740
00:42:07.025 --> 00:42:09.361
Was somebody there for you
when you got your period?

741
00:42:10.278 --> 00:42:11.404
Um...

742
00:42:12.030 --> 00:42:12.864
Yeah.

743
00:42:12.948 --> 00:42:14.282
-Yeah.
-Nice.

744
00:42:14.366 --> 00:42:15.200
-Good.
-Yeah.

745
00:42:15.283 --> 00:42:17.744
Oh. and look at you now.
My God. you're beautiful.

746
00:42:17.827 --> 00:42:20.288
-Thanks.
-How are you. honey? How's your dad?

747
00:42:20.372 --> 00:42:23.875
-You know what? Everybody's good.
-Is he dating anyone?

748
00:42:23.959 --> 00:42:27.337
-He... No.
-Oh. my God. What a waste.

749
00:42:27.420 --> 00:42:30.632
-He's so hot. He's like a smokestack.
-Mom.

750
00:42:30.715 --> 00:42:33.802
Do you know we only discovered Muskoka
because of your parents?

751
00:42:33.885 --> 00:42:37.430
We came up here with them one summer
before you guys were born.

752
00:42:37.514 --> 00:42:38.848
-[Rory] This is true.
-Really?

753
00:42:39.766 --> 00:42:42.018
Annie. your mother...

754
00:42:42.602 --> 00:42:47.482
Oh. my God. she was so upset that
she couldn't be with you and your brother.

755
00:42:48.275 --> 00:42:50.485
And honestly. I understand.

756
00:42:51.278 --> 00:42:54.072
I think that's what
finally led her to filing.

757
00:42:56.700 --> 00:43:00.287
Filing? Filing... Filing for what?

758
00:43:01.079 --> 00:43:04.332
For divorce from your... from your father.

759
00:43:04.416 --> 00:43:05.625
You knew that. right?

760
00:43:05.709 --> 00:43:07.627
[voices fading]

761
00:43:13.174 --> 00:43:14.009
Yeah.

762
00:43:15.218 --> 00:43:17.262
-Of course.
-Hey. Annie. baby. Hey.

763
00:43:17.345 --> 00:43:18.680
-Hi.
-How you doing?

764
00:43:18.763 --> 00:43:19.723
Hello.

765
00:43:19.806 --> 00:43:21.891
-[people whooping]
-Whoo!

766
00:43:21.975 --> 00:43:24.644
Um. Kaia Gerber isn't here.

767
00:43:24.728 --> 00:43:27.063
-Sorry. I haven't introduced--
-She got food poisoning

768
00:43:27.147 --> 00:43:29.274
-at the Beckhams' yesterday.
-Okay.

769
00:43:29.941 --> 00:43:31.860
I'm a drink away
from making out with a man.

770
00:43:31.943 --> 00:43:33.611
and we all know that I do not do that.

771
00:43:34.195 --> 00:43:37.407
-So. yeah. it's time to head.
-Yes. Let's do that.

772
00:43:37.490 --> 00:43:39.117
-It was really nice to see you.
-Fire.

773
00:43:39.200 --> 00:43:41.536
-It was really good to see you.
-So good to see you.

774
00:43:41.619 --> 00:43:44.622
-Bye. guys. Thank you for having us.
-Really good to see you.

775
00:43:44.706 --> 00:43:46.458
-I'm Oona. by the way.
-Thanks.

776
00:43:46.541 --> 00:43:48.626
-Oh. wow.
-Wow.

777
00:43:48.710 --> 00:43:50.045
Have a great night. Thank you.

778
00:43:50.128 --> 00:43:52.881
-[Oona] Yeah. okay.
-Be careful. Let's get you on the boat.

779
00:43:54.299 --> 00:43:55.425
[Annie] Okay.

780
00:43:55.508 --> 00:43:57.052
Is she the one
that makes out with all my friends?

781
00:43:57.135 --> 00:43:58.511
Yeah. Yeah. that's her.

782
00:43:59.596 --> 00:44:01.639
-Have I made out with her?
-Not yet.

783
00:44:01.723 --> 00:44:03.516
Let's get you inside.

784
00:44:22.035 --> 00:44:24.412
Um. thank you for walking me home.

785
00:44:24.496 --> 00:44:25.580
Yeah. Of course.

786
00:44:30.502 --> 00:44:35.215
Wait. so if I need something.
and I don't have service.

787
00:44:35.757 --> 00:44:38.259
-what do I...
-Just yell into the abyss.

788
00:44:38.343 --> 00:44:39.594
Oh!

789
00:44:39.677 --> 00:44:40.553
Sick. Okay.

790
00:44:41.429 --> 00:44:43.014
You're safe. though. I promise.

791
00:44:46.768 --> 00:44:48.728
Yeah. this is Canada. right?

792
00:44:49.938 --> 00:44:51.356
Nothing bad happens in Canada.

793
00:44:51.439 --> 00:44:54.734
Actually. no.
Bad shit happens. like. all the time.

794
00:44:55.819 --> 00:44:57.570
Just not on this island. though.

795
00:44:58.822 --> 00:45:00.323
-[chuckles]
-Okay.

796
00:45:02.158 --> 00:45:03.618
-Bye.
-Bye.

797
00:45:23.763 --> 00:45:25.557
-[girl] Hello?
-[gasps] Jesus!

798
00:45:30.728 --> 00:45:31.563
Who are you?

799
00:45:33.314 --> 00:45:34.149
Who are you?

800
00:45:36.443 --> 00:45:39.195
And what are you doing
in my grandfather's cottage?

801
00:45:51.249 --> 00:45:53.376
Connor. I have some very intense news.

802
00:45:53.585 --> 00:45:56.588
<i>Our mom. I think that she had</i>
<i>a secret biological daughter.</i>

803
00:45:56.671 --> 00:45:58.882
-Fuck!
-You said you'd be gone by the morning.

804
00:46:01.593 --> 00:46:03.386
[Ramona] <i>You said you were adopted?</i>

805
00:46:04.095 --> 00:46:05.930
-Yeah.
-So we're not related.

806
00:46:07.182 --> 00:46:09.058
-She hates me.
-Hey!

807
00:46:09.142 --> 00:46:11.686
She doesn't. Ramona is... She's complicated.

808
00:46:15.356 --> 00:46:18.401
Being here. it's like.
"I don't have a mom."

809
00:46:18.485 --> 00:46:21.571
I feel like I want
to punch a wall or something!

810
00:46:21.654 --> 00:46:25.116
Yeah. that's something we call rage.
It's better to make friends with it.

811
00:46:25.200 --> 00:46:27.535
It's only gonna get worse as you age. so...

812
00:46:30.163 --> 00:46:32.457
I just feel like
everything I knew about myself was wrong.

813
00:46:32.540 --> 00:46:33.875
[Rory] <i>That's a scary feeling.</i>

814
00:46:37.003 --> 00:46:39.255
It's good to be messy sometimes.
It's important.

815
00:46:40.882 --> 00:46:43.134
What do you know about my summer?
My summer.

816
00:46:43.760 --> 00:46:46.262
Well done. You just pushed me away
as far as you could.

817
00:46:47.096 --> 00:46:51.100
Your mom was the most fearless person
I've ever known.

818
00:46:54.103 --> 00:46:55.605
[Annie] <i>Growing up and changing</i>

819
00:46:55.688 --> 00:46:58.733
and feeling out of control.
it's really freaky.

820
00:46:59.567 --> 00:47:01.361
<i>But it's also pretty exciting.</i>

821
00:47:03.154 --> 00:47:04.948
Do you feel like you got
the answers you wanted?

822
00:47:05.031 --> 00:47:07.283
I feel like I've barely
scratched the surface.

823
00:47:10.286 --> 00:47:13.122
You said. "No more secrets."

824
00:47:14.305 --> 00:48:14.828
